{#- The image, as a figure so a caption stays attached to it. `src` is a
    `media` value: a path under the shared media directory goes through
    `media()`, which adds `/media`, and a page-relative path or a remote URL
    goes through `url()`, as it always did. On a sub-path install the
    base-path rewriter adds the deployment prefix.
    `data-canonical` and `data-part` are the markup contract every conforming
    theme's image carries. -#}
<figure class="image" data-canonical="image"><img data-part="image" src="{{ media(attrs.src) if attrs.src is startingwith("/") else url(attrs.src) }}" alt="{{ attrs.alt }}" loading="lazy">{% if attrs.caption %}<figcaption data-part="caption">{{ attrs.caption }}</figcaption>{% endif %}</figure>
